{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/958288-renown-gifts","id":958288,"title":"Renown Gifts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-26T10:49:41-07:00","id":958288,"title":"Renown Gifts","content":"I was curious how much Renown people give in a Shapeshifter campaign? I tend to try to give my characters opportunities to get 1 point of temporary Renown for every XP that they earn. The fact that my characters tend to lose 1 point of temporary Renown for every 2 points that they gain (one step back for every two steps forwards) means that they usually end up gaining 1 point of temporary Renown for every 2 XP that they get. <br /> <br /> That rate of advancement seems to allow for broader and forms of development, as characters do not always gain the right type of Renown for their advancement. My characters tend to gain an average of 80 XP before they reach Rank 2, 200 XP before they reach Rank 3, and 320 XP before they reach Rank 4 (I have never had anyone reach Rank 5 or Rank 6, but I imagine that they would have 440 XP before they reached Rank 5 and 540 XP before they reached Rank 6). Does that match the rate of advancement in anyone else's games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T12:06:09-07:00","id":958329,"title":"","content":"To be honest, i have never tracked how much XP - renown - rank has been earned...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T13:11:41-07:00","id":958377,"title":"","content":"I've never tried to tie Renown earned to XP gain. Renown gain is based on how a character behaves. That's it. I don't like the Revised/W20 expanded charts, because they create extremely fast Renown/Rank gain compared to XP, but that's simple enough to get around: just reward points more loosely with the charts solely as inspiration for what sorts of actions are good/bad for Renown, and how valued they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T17:17:43-07:00","id":958501,"title":"","content":"It also holds to roleplaying. For example my wife's black spiral. It's easy to rank up if you follow the spiral renown list (botw 1st) and just act like a complete asshole, so you demand bigger and better each time. That way you aren't getting to rank 5 off of petty actions but big events. Corrupting the entire northern hemisphere with wyrm taint by poisoning the monster energy drink production line may earn you high marks in cunning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T12:40:11-07:00","id":958841,"title":"","content":"Just cause they earn lots of temp renown, doesn't mean they automatically get to have the right of accomplishment cast on / for them..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T13:34:06-07:00","id":958873,"title":"","content":"It's not automatic, but it is expected. Besides simply asking politely (if you're earning a ton of Renown, why should anyone say no?), if for some reason you can't get it done like that, just challenge for it (and again, why would the MoC be a dick about this and not make it a challenge that drastically favors you over the rite master in question?), and sometimes the spirits will convert temporary to permanent Renown on their own if you're awesome enough (like having earned a ton of temp. Renown...).<br /> <br /> It's also kind of a dick move as the ST to hand out lots of temp. Renown and then have players sitting in piles of it they can't trade in for perm. Renown. If you want to slow things down, don't give out lots of temp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T17:26:24-07:00","id":958969,"title":"","content":"For my games, I usually only award renown at moots and so getting the temp renown converted to permanent seems simple enough afterwards. It's a rare thing to sit at 10 temp renown without the opportunity to have it converted over.<br /> <br /> On the OP and comparing renown to XP. I've never bothered to pay attention to the correlation between the 2. I don't know that there would be one. Some sessions are just RP heavy and aren't going to garner much in the way of renown, but you still get XP for them. Basically, the 2 (renown and XP) are completely different metrics to measure character advancement, and don't usually have anything to do with each other, from my point of view.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T14:18:46-07:00","id":959460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/958288-renown-gifts?p=958873#post958873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not automatic, but it is expected. Besides simply asking politely (if you're earning a ton of Renown, why should anyone say no?), if for some reason you can't get it done like that, just challenge for it (and again, why would the MoC be a dick about this and not make it a challenge that drastically favors you over the rite master in question?), and sometimes the spirits will convert temporary to permanent Renown on their own if you're awesome enough (like having earned a ton of temp. Renown...).<br /> <br /> It's also kind of a dick move as the ST to hand out lots of temp. Renown and then have players sitting in piles of it they can't trade in for perm. Renown. If you want to slow things down, don't give out lots of temp.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of the reasons i have denied the boost up to perm, is that they were still out in the field, OR had done something prior to getting sent out, to dick off the MoC.. So had to earn his (or her) good graces back to take said rite.<br /> <br /> <br /> Its like XP in adnd.. Can't earn it if you are still adventuring in the dungeon, ergo no level up.. Till you get back to base camp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T15:17:54-07:00","id":959512,"title":"","content":"The MoC doesn't decide if you can get the RoA unless you have to challenge for it. If the ritemaster agrees, the MoC doesn't have a say (beyond any other Garou that wants to heckle it). I think you're conflating things with how Rank challenges work.<br /> <br /> As well, the only reason that a RoA isn't usually done in the field, is that traditionally the RoA ritemaster should be higher Ranked than the Garou in question (but this is not actually a requirement of the Rite RAW).<br /> <br /> And this doesn't really have anything to do with the issue of the ST handling out Renown in excess of what the PCs can convert to permanent Renown. It doesn't matter if you wait until the end of a mission or quest to give it out, or as actions happen. You can't bank infinite amounts. Once you hit 10 temp, that's all you get to hold; that's where any sort of comparison to XP falls down. If your dungeon crawl generates 100 XP, 1,000 XP, or 100,000,000 XP it doesn't matter because there's no cap on how much XP you can hold before you get a chance to spend it. If your Garou are regularly earning ~20 temp Renown in a category before they can cash it in, it means most of their Renown is wasted. This tends to make the game less fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T15:57:11-07:00","id":959536,"title":"","content":"As others have stated, there is no direct tie between XP and Renown. It is possible to have a highly experienced character with very low renown. Or have high renown, but low XP simply because you've been lucky or politically favored. However, for the most part it is true that the higher XP the more likely the higher Renown.<br /> <br /> WTA20 pg 250 states that once you have 10 points of temporary Renown, you need to ask a Garou of your Rank or higher, who is not in the character's pack, to perform the Rite. If no one is willing or unable to perform the Rite, then the Garou can challenge an &quot;elder&quot; Garou (which I assume means a Garou of higher rank that you, not actually rank 5). While not explicitly stated, I assume that this Garou must also not be a member of one's pack.<br /> <br /> The intent is clearly that this is not something that needs to be done at the caern or through sept offices. However, the restriction of it not being done by one's pack member means that a neutral, unbiased third party has to approve. The Rite description seems very formal, and this is something that most Garou probably want done in front of everyone else during a moot. However, it does not need to be.<br /> <br /> I think in character, &quot;temporary renown&quot; means something the Garou can go up and boast in front of another Garou. It is an OOC accounting mechanism. There isn't really &quot;temporary renown&quot; in character. It is just a way the ST confirms to the PCs that this particular accomplishment is something worthy of boasting, and therefore once you have enough of such acts, decision, etc. the Garou Nation acknowledges your accomplishment. Other Garou learn this during moots (the Songs and Stories portion), and eventually when some elder Garou hears enough he decides to perform the rite. That this is done either through &quot;spirit confirmation&quot; via the Rite of Accomplishment, or by challenge against a higher ranked Garou means such boasts can be objectively verified to a degree.<br /> <br /> The system can of course be gamed, but I hold that more for flavor purposes or plot devices. Silver Fangs probably advance more quickly because they are given quicker and more opportunities to perform the Rite of Accomplishment. Bone Gnawers and Metis probably get less opportunities and have to challenge more. But it is a range. The system substantially works as it should. If there is some NPC jerk gaming the system to advance quicker then warranted, it should be because the ST is running a kind of plot or subplot or at least showcasing what kind of person that Garou is.<br /> <br /> One thing that is obvious is that the Garou who know the Rite of Accomplishment are very important in Garou society. They are probably very esteemed or trusted. This is not something you want to give to unscrupulous Garou or who have bad judgment. At best, this is given to really promising Fostern, but in actuality is probably reserved for Adren or higher. I imagine some tribes teach the rite more frequently among their tribe than others - Silver Fangs more likely know this than Bone Gnawers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T18:31:11-07:00","id":959604,"title":"","content":"I'd imagine tribes like the Bone Gnawers actually teach RoA more liberally, because it helps them maintain a power-base only proving their worth to other Gnawers instead of the standards of the more traditional Tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}